```js
function findFilter(dim){ return state.filters.find(f=>f.dim===dim); }
function setFilter(dim, f, action, source){ commit(action, source, ()=>{ 
  var i = state.filters.findIndex(x=>x.dim===dim);
  if(f===null){ if(i>=0) state.filters.splice(i,1); else return false? } ...
```
Careful: mutating inside commit; keep simple — always mutate, allow no-op.

```js
function toggleCatValue(dim, val, source){
  var f = findFilter(dim);
  var had = f && f.values.indexOf(val)>=0;
  commit((had?'过滤移除 ':'过滤 ')+DIM[dim].label+'='+val, source, function(){
    var cur = findFilter(dim);
    if(!cur){ state.filters.push({dim, kind:'cat', values:[val]}); return; }
    var vals = cur.values.slice(), k = vals.indexOf(val);
    if(k>=0){ vals.splice(k,1); if(!vals.length){ remove } else cur.values=vals; }
    else vals.push(val), cur.values=vals;
  });
}
function setRange(dim, lo, hi, source){ commit('过滤 '+DIM[dim].label+' ∈ ['+lo+', '+hi+']', source, ...) }
```

Quant bins: fixed domain per dim (DIM.min/max from data gen? Better compute from full records at init to be truthful): 
```js
var DOMAIN = {}; S.dims.filter(d=>d.type==='quant').forEach(d=>{ 
  var vs = S.records.map(r=>r[d.id]); DOMAIN[d.id] = {lo: Math.min(...vs), hi: Math.max(...vs), bins: 8};
});
```
But data.js already has min/max — recompute anyway for accuracy. Bins: width=(hi-lo)/8; bin index = min(7, floor((v-lo)/w)); label fmt by dec.

Axis spec:
```js
function axisVals(dim){ if cat return DIM[dim].values.slice(); else return bins array [{i,lo,hi,label}] }
function axisIndex(dim, v){ cat: values.indexOf(v); quant: min(7,max(0,floor((v-lo)/w))) }
```

